@startuml fault_handling_state
!theme cyborg
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam state {
 BackgroundColor #111826
 BorderColor #a9b8ca
 BackgroundColor<<implemented>> #1f3b2d
 BorderColor<<implemented>> #5fbf8a
 BackgroundColor<<documented>> #273241
 BorderColor<<documented>> #61738a
}
title Fault handling: recovery, indication and workflow admission are separate regions
hide empty description

state "Recovery episode: SERVER_CONNECTION_FAILURE and DEVICE_REGISTRATION_FAILURE only" as Recovery <<implemented>> {
 state "Available" as Available
 state "Unavailable episode" as Unavailable
 [*] --> Available
 Available --> Unavailable : preparation or registration fails\n/ log cause, request latch
 Unavailable --> Unavailable : automatic retry fails\n/ log only, no re-latch
 Unavailable --> Available : automatic retry succeeds\n/ episode ends, indication unchanged
}

state "Indication latch (red button LED)" as Indication <<documented>> {
 state "No error shown" as Clear
 state "Error latched" as Latched
 state "Shown until restart" as RestartLatched
 [*] --> Clear
 Clear --> Latched : catalogue error\n[row cleared by short press]
 Clear --> RestartLatched : catalogue error\n[row cleared by restart]
 Latched --> Latched : recovery succeeds\n[server, registration]\n/ stays latched
 Latched --> Clear : short press acknowledges\n/ ERROR_ACKNOWLEDGED flash
 RestartLatched --> RestartLatched : short press\n/ no effect
}

state "Workflow admission (CONTROL)" as Admission <<documented>> {
 state "Start permitted" as Permitted
 state "Start blocked, audio muted" as Blocked
 state "Blocked until restart" as BlockedRestart
 state "Deferred: listening continues" as Deferred
 [*] --> Permitted
 Permitted --> Permitted : Wi-Fi, server or registration error\n/ working audio kept, offline Start
 Permitted --> Blocked : other error [cleared by short press]\n/ stop workflow, mute, invalidate
 Permitted --> BlockedRestart : other error [cleared by restart]\n/ stop workflow, mute, invalidate
 Permitted --> BlockedRestart : audio error\n/ halt, every input blocked
 Permitted --> Deferred : non-audio halting error\nwhile listening / latch silently
 Deferred --> Blocked : manual Stop\n[cleared by short press] / show error
 Deferred --> BlockedRestart : manual Stop\n[cleared by restart] / show error
 Blocked --> Permitted : acknowledgement\n/ no Start, no retry
}

Recovery -[hidden]right-> Indication
Indication -[hidden]right-> Admission

legend bottom left
 The regions are coupled only by the catalogue error event and the acknowledgement; recovery success does not acknowledge.
 Green: implemented at integration 994ce24 (COMMUNICATION keeps an internal log-once flag per episode; it reports no catalogue code).
 Grey: documented, not implemented. CONTROL handles only the long press; there is no red LED driver and no short-press acknowledgement.
 Recovery episode: start cancellation alone raises no error; Wi-Fi and delivery errors have no episode rule.
 Indication: several errors show the highest priority, then the first latched. With a short-press-clearable error shown,
 the first short press acknowledges it; later presses Start and Stop (13 November). Errors during listening are shown after Stop.
 Admission: acknowledgement never starts, retries or changes an active workflow. Restart = reset button or power off/on.
endlegend
@enduml
